WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.514
A thread begins as almost nothing: loose fibre, light enough to drift.

2
00:00:04.849 --> 00:00:13.760
Drawn together, those fibres align. Tension gives them direction. Twist gives them strength. A strand becomes something that can carry continuity.

3
00:00:14.121 --> 00:00:26.417
Now the loom introduces structure. Warp establishes the path. Weft crosses it, one passage at a time. The shuttle moves forward, the pattern remembers what came before, and separate moments become cloth.

4
00:00:26.751 --> 00:00:28.806
DHAGO treats video the same way.

5
00:00:29.094 --> 00:00:46.783
Time is not painted onto a decorative timeline. Real media time drives the woven state. Chapter boundaries become sections of the textile. Seeking moves the shuttle. Captions, keyboard controls, responsive layouts and reduced-motion behavior remain part of the same accessible player.

6
00:00:47.169 --> 00:00:55.683
At thirty-two seconds, warp meets weft. Move backward and the fabric returns toward thread. Move forward and the structure resolves again.

7
00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:59.899
The picture tells the process. The player exposes the mechanism.

8
00:01:00.251 --> 00:01:02.817
From fibre, to thread, to woven time.
